    "menu.settings": "Settings",
    // note
    "note.0-0.dix_ans_plus_tot": "Ten years earlier. The Chancellery asked me to simplify this valley.",
    "note.0-0.me_souviens_plus_nom": "I no longer remember the name. That is the price.",
    "note.0-0.route_passe_par_village": "The road runs through the village. One line, and it no longer does.",
    "note.1-1.crue_deux_cartes_tirent": "The flood. Two maps pull this ford each their own way, and the water decides.",
    "note.1-1.hachures_frissonnent_bord_bief": "The hachures shiver at the edge of the millrace. Next time, the ground will waver.",
    "note.1-1.oudine_gue_appelle_gue": "Oudine: “The ford isn't called \"ford\". It is named after the women who crossed it with a child on their hip.”",
    "note.1-1.suivent_route_plus_seche": "They follow the driest road. Always. I'm the one who taught them.",
    "note.1-2.crue_encore_echassiers_rient": "The flood again. The Stilt-walkers laugh in the water.",
    "note.1-2.gens_bocage_leurs_vaches": "Hedgerow folk, their cows ahead of them. They are looking for the Refuge. Each one carries a name.",
    "note.1-2.jalonneurs_regardent_pente_regardent": "The Markers don't watch the slope. They watch the Mother Stone.",
    "note.1-2.mortier_fait_difference_entre": "The mortar can't tell a seal from an apron.",
    "note.1-2.nom_plus_dans_role": "One more name in Oudine's Roll.",
    "note.1-3.echassier_fredonne_connais_cet": "A Stilt-walker hums. I know that tune: Oudine's lullaby.",
    "note.1-3.eux_sous_mes_tours": "Not them. Not under my towers.",
    "note.1-3.oudine_ce_champ_appelle": "Oudine: “This field is called Pain-Perdu because we lost it twice. Put it on your map, or I'll keep telling you until winter.”",
    "note.1-3.role_grave_reste_savoir": "The Roll is engraved. Now, where to put those who flee.",
    "note.1-4.boeufs_paniquent_fuit_tours": "The oxen panic. It shies from the towers: we can drive it back.",
    "note.1-4.garde_ma_facon_faire": "He kept my way of drawing the Vs.",
    "note.1-4.gast_borne_quatre_plantez": "Gast: “Stone four! Plant it! The rest will follow.”",
    "note.1-4.grande_chaine_effondre_dans": "The Great Chain collapses into the millrace. In its chests, marching orders for the Passes, signed “C. Vass”.",
    "note.1-4.grande_chaine_suit_leve": "The Great Chain follows a survey. Mine, ten years ago, stone for stone.",
    "note.1-4.ma_main_borne_dix": "That's my hand on the stone. Ten years, and the ink hasn't faded.",
    "note.1-4.moulin_decouvert_empire_grave": "The Mill is exposed. The Empire carves its own stone on the millstone: a Name fades from the Roll.",
    "note.1-4.oudine_se_tait_dit": "Oudine is silent. She says nothing more about the Roll.",
    "note.1-4.oudine_vu_passer_chacun": "Oudine saw every one of them pass. She will speak, later.",
    "note.1-4.traversent_zone_tir_savais": "They cross the line of fire. I knew it when I set the Refuge here.",
    "note.2-1.gel_lac_devient_route": "The Freeze. The lake becomes a road, and it isn't ours who take it.",
    "note.2-1.gens_col_grimpent_ce": "The Pass Folk climb what the Chainmen go around. Two readings of one slope.",
    "note.2-1.givre_court_lac_demain": "Frost runs over the lake. Tomorrow, it will bear weight.",
    "note.2-1.hardes_lisent_pente_elles": "The Herds don't read the slope. They read my towers, and pass where I'm not looking.",
    "note.2-1.hesse_tu_veux_savoir": "Hesse: “You want to know who the enemy is? Look at who has cold feet in both columns.”",
    "note.2-1.refuge_tient_hesse_compte": "The Refuge holds. Hesse counts her people, then mine, and says nothing.",
    "note.2-2.avalanche_couloir_sud_existe": "The avalanche. The south gully now exists only on my map.",
    "note.2-2.corentin_donne_moi_retire": "Corentin: “Give them to me and I'll pull back the 4th. It's arithmetic, Nève.”",
    "note.2-2.corniche_tient_deux_couloirs": "The ledge hangs on two gullies. The south one is shorter, and the snow knows it.",
    "note.2-2.gel_encore_gens_col": "The Freeze again. The Pass Folk cross the lake without even looking down.",
    "note.2-2.neige_pend_dessus_couloir": "Snow hangs over the south gully. I draw nothing under it any more.",
    "note.2-2.tout_arithmetique_ca_probleme": "Everything is arithmetic. That's the problem.",
    "note.2-3.charrette_passe_col_hesse": "A cart crosses the pass. Hesse doesn't look back.",
    "note.2-3.convoi_passe_sous_glace": "The convoy is through. Under the melted ice, hachures no one drew.",
    "note.2-3.deux_routes_se_croisent": "Two roads cross in the middle of the pass: theirs and hers. I draw only one at a time.",
    "note.2-3.gel_convoi_pourrait_couper": "The Freeze. The convoy could cut across the lake. So could the Herds.",
    "note.2-3.hesse_m_regardee_compte": "Hesse didn't look at me. She counted her carts, twice, and struck a name from her register.",
    "note.2-3.hesse_passe_gens_passe": "Hesse: “I don't smuggle people. I smuggle stories that still have legs.”",
    "note.2-3.mortier_lit_passeports_hesse": "The mortar doesn't read passports. Hesse won't forgive me either.",
    "note.erased": "I scratched out “{}”. Only the square is left.",
